PR #156  overall: potential_risk
Spec: Mismatched Zilsd alignment flags cause the compiler to emit 64-bit memory accesses at 4-byte alignment targeting hardware that requires 8-byte natural alignment, risking silent data corruption or unexpected traps.
  [OK] arch/riscv/include/asm/hwcap.h:111-111  (none — macro definition)
      Trivial constant definition (RISCV_ISA_EXT_ZILSD = 102). Correctly enumerated in sequence with no logic to be right or wrong.
  [RISK] arch/riscv/include/uapi/asm/hwprobe.h:87-87  (none — UAPI bit definition)
      Defines RISCV_HWPROBE_EXT_ZILSD as bit 61. The hwprobe API exposes a binary yes/no for ZILSD support but provides no sub-key to differentiate hardware alignment requirements (word-align vs strict-align) for Zilsd's 64-bit register-pair accesses on RV32. Userspace sees the extension is available but cannot determine whether -mzilsd-word-align or -mzilsd-strict-align is safe for this core. The generic RISCV_HWPROBE_KEY_MISALIGNED_SCALAR_PERF key reports scalar (native-width) misalignment behavior, not the Zilsd-specific 64-bit-alignment-on-32-bit-base constraint.
  [RISK] arch/riscv/include/uapi/asm/kvm.h:196-196  (none — KVM UAPI enum)
      Enum entry KVM_RISCV_ISA_EXT_ZILSD in KVM's ISA extension register UAPI. When a host exposes ZILSD to a guest via KVM, the guest may compile with incorrect alignment assumptions (-mzilsd-word-align vs -mzilsd-strict-align) since KVM provides no sub-attribute to communicate the alignment flavor the host hardware enforces.
  [OK] arch/riscv/kernel/cpufeature.c:246-253  riscv_ext_zilsd_validate
      Correctly rejects Zilsd on CONFIG_64BIT since Zilsd is an RV32-only extension per the ISA spec. The validate callback correctly gates on the ISA architectural constraint. Alignment-flavor validation is a runtime probing concern, not a detection-time concern, so this validator is not the right place to enforce it.
  [OK] arch/riscv/kernel/cpufeature.c:255-266  riscv_ext_zclsd_validate
      Correctly enforces Zclsd's dependency chain: requires ZILSD and ZCA to both be available, and also rejects on CONFIG_64BIT. This validator correctly models the ISA-mandated dependency graph.
